IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`
IMPORT `cat-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `cat-part2-div2-3-microchip-sterilise`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 2 DIVISION 4: TRANSFER OF OWNERSHIP OF CATS
-- (ss 22-24) and DIVISION 5: CHANGES TO RECORDED INFORMATION (s 25), with
-- Cat Regulations 2012 reg 19.
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 313-348; inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt
-- lines 206-207.

§ `Part 2 — Registration, identification and sterilisation of cats`

§§ `Division 4 — Transfer of ownership of cats`

§§§ `22. Terms used`

-- s 22: "purchaser, of a cat, means the person to whom the cat is
-- transferred; seller, of a cat, means the person by whom the cat is
-- transferred." A Transfer record names both. "transfer" itself is s 3(1),
-- and includes giving a cat away and reclaiming it from a cat management
-- facility (cat-part1-preliminary.l4).

§§§ `23. Transfer of ownership of cats`

-- s 23(3): "This section, or a part of this section prescribed, does not
-- apply — (a) in respect of a cat that belongs to a class of cats, if any,
-- prescribed; or (b) in the circumstances, if any, prescribed."
-- reg 19: "The provisions of section 23(1) and (2) of the Act do not apply
-- if a cat is being transferred to an organisation or person set out in
-- regulation 9."
--
-- FORK F-12: "an organisation or person set out in regulation 9" is read as
-- the bodies reg 9 names — Cat Haven, the RSPCA WA, the three SAFE entities
-- (reg 9(1)) and the Commonwealth department (reg 9(2)(c)) — and the
-- custodians it describes, a cat management facility and veterinary
-- premises (reg 9(2)(d), (e)). A private foster carer is not "set out": reg
-- 9(3) describes a placement, not a person. The other reading, that a
-- foster carer placed by one of those bodies is a person set out in reg 9,
-- would exempt transfers into such foster care too.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 19, reg 9
GIVEN o IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an organisation set out in reg 9` o IF
        o EQUALS `Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven`
    ..  o EQUALS `The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia`
    ..  o EQUALS `Saving Animals from Euthanasia Incorporated`
    ..  o EQUALS `S.A.F.E. Hedland Inc`
    ..  o EQUALS `Saving Animals from Euthanasia Busselton Inc`
    OR  o EQUALS `the Commonwealth Department administering the Biosecurity Act 2015`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 23(3); Cat Regulations 2012 reg 19
GIVEN t IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(1) and (2) do not apply to` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `transferred to`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST c  THEN CONSIDER c
                      WHEN `an organisation` o          THEN `an organisation set out in reg 9` o
                      WHEN `a cat management facility`  THEN TRUE
                      WHEN `veterinary premises`        THEN TRUE
                      WHEN `a private person`           THEN FALSE

-- s 23(1): "A person must not transfer a cat that is not microchipped
-- unless, at the time of the transfer, the person is satisfied that a
-- certificate referred to in section 14(2) applies in respect of the cat."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 23(1)
GIVEN t   IS A Transfer
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(1) is contravened by` t `of` cat IF
        `the law is encoded for` (t's `date of the transfer`)
    AND NOT `microchipped` cat
    AND NOT "unless ... satisfied that a s 14(2) certificate applies" ... t's `seller satisfied a microchipping certificate applies`
    AND NOT "(3), reg 19" ... `s 23(1) and (2) do not apply to` t

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 23(1) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 23(1) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

-- s 23(2): "A person must not transfer a cat that is not sterilised unless,
-- at the time of the transfer — (a) the person is satisfied that — (i) a
-- certificate referred to in section 18(2)(a) applies in respect of the cat;
-- or (ii) the purchaser is an approved cat breeder and the purchaser is
-- purchasing the cat for the purpose of breeding; or (iii) the cat belongs
-- to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation; or (b) a
-- voucher is given to the purchaser by the person to enable the purchaser
-- to have the cat sterilised at a later date by a veterinarian at no cost
-- to the purchaser."
--
-- Each limb of (a) is the SELLER's satisfaction, an input; (iii) can never
-- be met, because no class is prescribed (cat-part2-div2-3-...l4, s 18(2)(c)).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 23(2)
GIVEN t   IS A Transfer
      cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(2) is contravened by` t `of` cat IF
        `the law is encoded for` (t's `date of the transfer`)
    AND NOT `sterilised` cat
    AND NOT `an exception in (a) or (b)`
    AND NOT "(3), reg 19" ... `s 23(1) and (2) do not apply to` t
    WHERE
        `an exception in (a) or (b)` MEANS
                "(a)" ... `the seller is satisfied of (i), (ii) or (iii)`
            OR  "(b)" ... t's `voucher for later sterilisation at no cost given`
        `the seller is satisfied of (i), (ii) or (iii)` MEANS
                "(i)"   ... t's `seller satisfied a sterilisation certificate applies`
            ..  "(ii)"  ... t's `seller satisfied the purchaser is an approved breeder buying to breed`
            OR  "(iii)" ... `belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` cat

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 23(2) "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 23(2) — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§§ `24. Notice to be given of transfer of cat`

-- s 24: "Within 7 days after the transfer of a cat, the seller of the cat
-- must give notice in writing — (a) to the local government with which the
-- cat is registered, of — (i) the name and address of the purchaser of the
-- cat; and (ii) any other changes to the information prescribed under
-- section 12(3) in respect of the cat; and (b) to the microchip database
-- company for that cat, of — (i) the name and address of the purchaser of
-- the cat; and (ii) any other changes to the information prescribed under
-- section 15 in respect of the cat."
--
-- Limb (a) has a local government to notify only if the cat is registered;
-- limb (b) a database company only if the cat is microchipped (s 3(1)
-- "microchip database company" (b): the company that keeps that cat's record).
-- The two notices are owed at once, not one after the other: RAND.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 24(a)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 24(a) — notice to the local government, counted in days from the transfer` MEANS
    PARTY `the seller of the cat`
    MUST  `give the local government notice of the purchaser and of other changes`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the seller of the cat` BECAUSE "s 24(a): the local government was not notified of the purchaser within 7 days after the transfer"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 24(b)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 24(b) — notice to the microchip database company, counted in days from the transfer` MEANS
    PARTY `the seller of the cat`
    MUST  `give the microchip database company notice of the purchaser and of other changes`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the seller of the cat` BECAUSE "s 24(b): the microchip database company was not notified of the purchaser within 7 days after the transfer"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 24
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor `Act required`
`s 24 — the seller's duties, counted in days from the transfer` MEANS
        `s 24(a) — notice to the local government, counted in days from the transfer`
    RAND `s 24(b) — notice to the microchip database company, counted in days from the transfer`


@ref Cat Act 2011 s 24
GIVEN d                                   IS A DATE
      t                                   IS A Transfer
      cat                                 IS A Cat
      `notice to the local government on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `notice to the database company on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      holidays                            IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24 is contravened, as at` d `, by` t `of` cat `, notices given on` `notice to the local government on` `and` `notice to the database company on` `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND (    "(a)" ...     `registered` cat `on` (t's `date of the transfer`)
                       AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (t's `date of the transfer`) `, done on` `notice to the local government on` `, as at` d `given` holidays
         OR  "(b)" ...     `microchipped` cat
                       AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (t's `date of the transfer`) `, done on` `notice to the database company on` `, as at` d `given` holidays)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 24 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 24 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000

§§ `Division 5 — Changes to recorded information`

§§§ `25. Notice to be given of changes to recorded information`

-- s 25: "The owner of a cat must give notice in writing — (a) to the local
-- government with which the cat is registered, if there is a change to any
-- of the information prescribed under section 12(3) in respect of the cat;
-- and (b) to the microchip database company for that cat, if there is a
-- change to any of the information prescribed under section 15 in respect
-- of the cat, within 7 days after the change to the information."
-- The prescribed information is reg 16 (register) and reg 17 (database).
-- (the type is declared in cat-domain.l4)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25
GIVEN cat                  IS A Cat
      ch                   IS A `Change to recorded information`
      p                    IS A Person
      `notice to the local government on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `notice to the database company on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      d                    IS A DATE
      holidays             IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25 is contravened as to` cat `after` ch `by` p `, notices given on` `notice to the local government on` `and` `notice to the database company on` `, as at` d `given` holidays IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `an owner of` cat `on` (ch's `date of the change`) `:` p
    AND (    "(a)" ...     `registered` cat `on` (ch's `date of the change`)
                       AND ch's `changes reg 16 register information`
                       AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (ch's `date of the change`) `, done on` `notice to the local government on` `, as at` d `given` holidays
         OR  "(b)" ...     `microchipped` cat
                       AND ch's `changes reg 17 database information`
                       AND `not done within` 7 `days after` (ch's `date of the change`) `, done on` `notice to the database company on` `, as at` d `given` holidays)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 25 "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 25 — maximum fine` MEANS 5000
